-- title:
--   Finite support of orders in a finite parameter extension
-- statement:
--   For a finite extension of the field generated by a transcendental parameter, a fixed element has nonzero order at only finitely many normalized places. This supplies the finite-support conjunct in the parameter case. The definition bundle defines the places and orders; the new argument is to classify the places of the one-variable function field and show that a fixed element has only finitely many zeros and poles. This also covers f = 0, whose order is everywhere zero. The remaining work is the place classification and its connection to the valuation type.
-- source:
--   openai/math Approximation FibreNormalRigidity: nonconstant fibre coordinates imply quantitative contact bound.

